-- REQ-001 / REQ-011 subprocess ----------------------------------------
recorder: two records, neither written by the router. The SHELL records the pid it
          launched, through $!. The CHILD records its own getppid(), which is the
          kernel's answer to who spawned it, into a file under a path passed in the
          environment and never read back by the product. If those two agree, the
          spawn is attributed by two parties that cannot have coordinated.

          A ps(1) sample runs alongside as a third, best-effort reading. It usually
          misses: the index verb spawns, handshakes and exits inside one scheduling
          quantum. Two earlier versions of this witness depended on ps alone and could
          report only that the child had a parent, not whose child it was.
